Kind: ablation
Issue: #659
Takes out: the report lock's hold on the other processors -- cons_report_elsewhere() answers that nobody holds a report, as before 0de054a5, so cons_wire_byte() never waits and cons_tx_one() never leaves a byte in the ring while another processor reports, and the target's report goes to the wire byte by byte between the boot processor's lines; two reports still take turns in cons_report_begin()
Run: --entry 0 600 -smp 4
Over: 659-widen-tick-in-flight.patch
Over: 659-widen-unclaimed-report.patch
Expect: UrMach x86-64: trap unclaimed interrupt \((v[^e]|ve[^c]|vec[^t]|vect[^o]|vecto[^r]|vector[^ ]|vector [^0]|vector 0[^x]|vector 0x[0-9a-f]*[^0-9a-f,])
Expect: ^  rip .* rsp +[^0 ]
Expect: ^([^U]|U[^r]|Ur[^M]).*no handler — halted
Expect: [ ]{2}(r[a-d]x|r[sd]i|r[bs]p|r[0-9]+|cs|ss|cr3) +0x([0-9a-f]{0,15}[^0-9a-f]|[0-9a-f]{16}([^ [:cntrl:]]| [^ ]))
Expect: ^  r[a-z0-9]+ +0x[0-9a-z ]*[^0-9a-z <[:cntrl:]]
Expect: UrMach x86-64: trap ([^a-zS]|u[a-z0-9 (),]*[^a-z0-9 (),[:cntrl:]])
Note: the fifth and sixth Expect lines say what the four before them list, as a property rather than as shapes seen (#695).  The fifth: a line that begins with an r register carries, before any "<", a byte no register line has.  On GitHub's run 38449528373 (9c1d9aaa, TCG) this patch broke the report in seven places, its register lines each in a field's name, in a separator, or over a field's two leading spaces; none of the four matched, ablate.sh said NOT CAUGHT, and the fifth matches the rax and r10 lines.  A "<" is not such a byte: ddb's display after a panic puts a symbol beside rip, "rip    0x... <Debugger+0x...>", on a whole line.  The sixth: the report's first line carries a byte its whole form never has -- right after "trap ", one that is neither a lower-case letter nor the S of SIMD, every trap's name beginning with one of those, or after this trap's "u" one outside the lower-case letters, digits, blank, parentheses and comma that "unclaimed interrupt (vector 0x..., error 0x...)" is made of.  On pavillion under KVM (61bcabb7) the first line broke inside "unclaimed" in three boots of three, and every line after it too, so none of the five matched.  A report whose only break takes a line's leading "  r" away, or falls in the cs line, is still seen by none of the six; nor is a first line broken before its "trap " is whole, which the sixth cannot tell from the many whole lines that begin "UrMach x86-64: t" -- at c8198904 one boot under KVM broke there, after "tra", and was caught by the third, fourth and fifth lines, the rest of its report being broken too.
Note: the first four Expect lines are a report another processor's bytes broke, each as it was seen: before the lock, on GitHub's run 38205894781 (8eda7df9), the first line in all four boots under KVM, the rip line and the halt line in one boot each of four under TCG; with it taken out, on OMEGA (0872b14e), a field of a register line in all four boots, the first field or a later one, and the halt line in both under TCG; a line's last field ends in the log's \r, which [:cntrl:] keeps out.  Whole reports match none of them: victus's eight with the lock (2d832e72), OMEGA's four fixed boots, and the 140 logs of a merge test (batch 19).  The fixed arm fails on the trap the two widens hold open, as 659-vector-back-zero's ablated arm does: what it must not show is the Expect

